      "text": "Inference in AI refers to the process of running a trained model to generate predictions, completions, or embeddings for new inputs. It is the operational phase where models serve real-world requests, distinct from training. Inference systems optimize for latency, throughput, and cost, employing techniques like kv-caching, quantization, batching, and speculative decoding. The term also denotes the serving stack — model loaders, schedulers, and APIs — that powers production applications."
